      "latin": "superbus, superba, superbum",
      "status": "recommended",
      "period": "classical",
      "gloss": "proud, haughty, arrogant",
      "grammar": "adjective",
      "evidence": [
        "Plaut. Asin. 470: <span lang=\"la\">nōn decet superbum esse hominem servom</span>",
        "Cic. Att. 8.4.1: <span lang=\"la\">superbum sē praebuit</span>",
        "Traupman 326"
      ],
      "comment": "The usual word, always in a bad sense in classical prose: one who thinks himself above others, and so rude and overbearing (Lewis &amp; Short). The noun is <span lang=\"la\">superbia</span>, pride. In poetry it can also be “proud of, splendid” (see proud, pleased)."
    },
    {
